          "text": "Chapter 1: Energy Reserves and Potential Highlights of reserves in India 1.1 Coal Reserves India is home to one of the largest proven coal reserves in the world. As of total estimated coal reserves were 400.7 billion tonnes , showing an addition of tonnes compared to the previous year. This marks a growth of 2.90% in total during the year 2024-25(P) over the previous year (2023-24) (Table 1.1). The distribution of coal reserves in India is concentrated in a few states like Odisha , Jharkhand and Chhattisgarh. These three states account for approximately 70% of the total coal reserves in the country. Out of the total reserves in the country, proven reserves i.e. economically viable and geologically confirmed account for approximately 55% of the total estimated coal reserves as depicted in the figure 1.1 . 1.2 Lignite Reserves The total estimated reserves of lignite as on 01-04-2025 stood at 47.371 showing an increase of tonnes over the previous marks an increase of 0.15% reserves during the year compared to 2023-24 (Table highest reserves of lignite the state of Tamil Nadu (79%) Out of the total lignite country, proven reserves account for approximately total lignite reserves in India the figure 1.2 . * Brief about the Proved, Inferred and Indicated has been given under Annexure-I. Proved 55% Indicated 37% Inferred 8% Fig 1.1 Estimated Reserves of Coal India as on 01.04.2025 Total Estimated reserves = 400.715 Billion Proved, 17% Indicated, 53% Inferred, 30% Fig 1.2 Estimated Reserves of Lignite in India as on 01.04.2025 Total Estimated reserves =47.371 Billion Tonnes",
